1
00:00:36,227 --> 00:00:38,563
I got mugged. I thought it
was the end for me.

2
00:00:38,688 --> 00:00:40,607
Good thing a woman saved me.

3
00:00:40,774 --> 00:00:42,692
Hey.

4
00:00:45,904 --> 00:00:47,822
You're not my type, bro.

5
00:00:48,531 --> 00:00:49,949
Where's my painting?

6
00:00:49,949 --> 00:00:50,842
Ah, the painting?

7
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:51,843
You took my painting?

8
00:00:51,868 --> 00:00:52,452
Not me.

9
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:53,161
Look, miss.

10
00:00:53,161 --> 00:00:54,204
I'll prove to you

11
00:00:54,204 --> 00:00:55,955
that I'm not working
with the thieves

12
00:00:55,955 --> 00:00:57,165
who stole your painting.

13
00:00:57,165 --> 00:00:58,875
There's no getting it back anymore.

14
00:00:58,952 --> 00:01:00,787
Yeye wants a balloon!

15
00:01:00,819 --> 00:01:04,865
O, to the M, to the G!
What is this?

16
00:01:05,006 --> 00:01:06,633
Where am I this time?

17
00:01:06,633 --> 00:01:09,135
Ugh! What is this?

18
00:01:09,135 --> 00:01:10,428
I can't be mistaken.

19
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:14,683
You're the one in the picture
with Ate Ysa from the town hall.

20
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:17,560
Hey, are you stalking her?

21
00:01:20,939 --> 00:01:22,232
Estong!

22
00:01:28,071 --> 00:01:29,739
- It's just me now. Ysa.
- A different name?

23
00:01:30,156 --> 00:01:31,449
I have...

24
00:01:31,449 --> 00:01:33,618
Dissociative Identity Disorder.

25
00:02:52,331 --> 00:02:56,075
My different personalities
come out because...

26
00:02:59,245 --> 00:03:01,873
of the traumas I went through as a child.

27
00:03:04,266 --> 00:03:05,935
My doctor said,

28
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,505
they're not just imaginary friends.

29
00:03:11,341 --> 00:03:14,469
It's not like I can just switch
personalities whenever I want.

30
00:03:15,345 --> 00:03:17,889
They're a part of me that keeps me alive,

31
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:22,268
to help me face things that
are hard for me to deal with.

32
00:03:24,512 --> 00:03:26,430
My different personalities

33
00:03:27,057 --> 00:03:29,643
are my mind's way of keeping me safe.

34
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,905
Can I ask

35
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:36,157
what triggers them to come out?

36
00:03:38,409 --> 00:03:39,395
Trigger?

37
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,553
You're such bad luck!

38
00:03:40,578 --> 00:03:41,955
You have no shame!

39
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:45,416
You bastard!

40
00:03:46,626 --> 00:03:49,521
It's my fault, right? I'm always
the one to blame?!

41
00:03:49,546 --> 00:03:50,505
It depends.

42
00:03:51,261 --> 00:03:53,508
It can be due to a lot of stress,

43
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,718
fear or anger.

44
00:03:57,428 --> 00:04:01,641
Sometimes even extreme happiness or
excitement can trigger them.

45
00:04:02,183 --> 00:04:03,226
Even something

46
00:04:03,434 --> 00:04:04,686
as simple as a smell,

47
00:04:05,353 --> 00:04:06,729
a person, a place...

48
00:04:07,557 --> 00:04:08,690
or memories—

49
00:04:08,690 --> 00:04:09,399
Come on, let's see.

50
00:04:09,399 --> 00:04:10,733
can be a trigger for me.

51
00:04:14,279 --> 00:04:15,905
How many personalities do you have?

52
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:20,326
The ones you've met...

53
00:04:22,829 --> 00:04:25,665
are four of my six dominant personalities.

54
00:04:25,957 --> 00:04:26,878
What?

55
00:04:27,678 --> 00:04:28,659
Six?

56
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:30,628
Kuya.

57
00:04:31,588 --> 00:04:34,048
- Are you stalking your ex again?
- This is different.

58
00:04:34,257 --> 00:04:35,758
This is different, okay?

59
00:04:39,929 --> 00:04:40,972
Do you remember

60
00:04:41,347 --> 00:04:42,557
the woman who saved me?

61
00:04:43,057 --> 00:04:43,600
Mhm.

62
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:45,096
We saw each other again.

63
00:04:45,393 --> 00:04:46,811
I learned something about her.

64
00:04:48,104 --> 00:04:49,314
What is it? Uh...

65
00:04:50,315 --> 00:04:53,359
Is she loving, sweet, and caring?

66
00:04:55,737 --> 00:04:56,946
Bro, it's complicated.

67
00:04:58,281 --> 00:05:00,867
Complicated? Why?
What's the problem?

68
00:05:03,036 --> 00:05:04,412
Pops, she has a...

69
00:05:04,913 --> 00:05:06,414
mental health condition.

70
00:05:07,582 --> 00:05:09,026
She has different personalities.

71
00:05:14,255 --> 00:05:15,256
I see.

72
00:05:15,506 --> 00:05:18,343
I think I saw this in a movie once.

73
00:05:18,718 --> 00:05:21,237
You know, the one about multiple or
split personalities?

74
00:05:21,262 --> 00:05:21,651
Kuya.

75
00:05:21,676 --> 00:05:23,656
Bro, bro, bro. You're
using the wrong term.

76
00:05:23,681 --> 00:05:25,683
- The correct term is—
- But kuya, I saw that in a movie.

77
00:05:25,683 --> 00:05:28,519
I know. But that's not the right term.
The right term is...

78
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:32,190
Dissociative Identity Disorder or DID.

79
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:35,008
"Split" and "multiple"
aren't the right terms.

80
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:36,326
"D.I.D."?

81
00:05:36,861 --> 00:05:38,279
So that's actually a real thing?

82
00:05:38,488 --> 00:05:42,742
I've never met anyone with a condition
like that before.

83
00:05:43,326 --> 00:05:44,285
Actually, Pops...

84
00:05:44,786 --> 00:05:46,955
I first saw her here in our cafe.

85
00:05:46,955 --> 00:05:48,498
Do you remember the woman
who was painting there?

86
00:05:49,457 --> 00:05:50,959
Let me stay here!

87
00:05:51,376 --> 00:05:52,502
- I want to jump!
- You're so heavy, kuya.

88
00:05:52,502 --> 00:05:53,753
Excuse us, miss.

89
00:05:54,963 --> 00:05:57,423
Oh, that was her?

90
00:05:57,882 --> 00:05:58,690
Huh!

91
00:05:58,716 --> 00:06:00,927
She's one of our regular customers.

92
00:06:00,927 --> 00:06:02,428
She's the one you bothered?

93
00:06:04,681 --> 00:06:06,099
That was the first time I saw her.

94
00:06:06,099 --> 00:06:08,643
Well, duh. You've been
gone for a while, Kuya.

95
00:06:10,353 --> 00:06:12,397
I knew it. I really knew it.

96
00:06:12,647 --> 00:06:14,357
Whenever she orders,

97
00:06:14,565 --> 00:06:15,900
she uses a different names every time.

98
00:06:16,401 --> 00:06:17,443
I know. There's Yeye,

99
00:06:17,485 --> 00:06:19,988
Cacai, Tristan, and Bogart.

100
00:06:20,282 --> 00:06:21,282
Wow.

101
00:06:21,364 --> 00:06:24,283
So you've already met
four of her personalities?

102
00:06:24,617 --> 00:06:25,578
Just wow.

103
00:06:26,172 --> 00:06:27,923
Every personality

104
00:06:29,622 --> 00:06:31,124
has their own mind,

105
00:06:33,084 --> 00:06:35,169
actions, and way of speaking.

106
00:06:37,755 --> 00:06:40,258
Even their likes and
dislikes are different.

107
00:06:40,758 --> 00:06:42,635
So that's why it felt like

108
00:06:42,969 --> 00:06:44,470
I was talking to different people.

109
00:06:45,388 --> 00:06:46,556
That's why...

110
00:06:47,765 --> 00:06:49,851
sometimes I can't remember certain things.

111
00:06:51,519 --> 00:06:53,855
Because when another
personality takes over,

112
00:06:54,594 --> 00:06:57,597
I can't just access those memories.

113
00:06:57,622 --> 00:07:01,208
I hope someone wrote an entry.

114
00:07:04,032 --> 00:07:06,034
Especially when it's someone I don't get
along with.

115
00:07:06,864 --> 00:07:08,688
That's why I want us all to...

116
00:07:08,953 --> 00:07:12,498
get along, so everything's easier and we're
all more aware.

117
00:07:13,082 --> 00:07:14,039
That's it.

118
00:07:14,876 --> 00:07:17,170
Can your condition be...

119
00:07:17,837 --> 00:07:19,213
medically treated?

120
00:07:19,464 --> 00:07:22,967
It's mostly through therapy sessions.

121
00:07:24,043 --> 00:07:26,462
D.I.D. doesn't just simply go away.

122
00:07:27,388 --> 00:07:29,182
It can last a lifetime.

123
00:07:30,767 --> 00:07:33,394
That's why I really want
us all to get along because...

124
00:07:33,519 --> 00:07:35,521
we're not enemies.

125
00:07:36,606 --> 00:07:38,900
We have to learn to work together because,

126
00:07:40,151 --> 00:07:41,152
after all...

127
00:07:43,071 --> 00:07:44,822
we're all just one person.

128
00:07:49,744 --> 00:07:52,497
Looks like you've already set your sights
on someone new.

129
00:07:53,069 --> 00:07:55,046
What about your Australian dream?

130
00:07:55,595 --> 00:07:57,764
I don't think I can handle
another complicated woman, bro.

131
00:07:57,877 --> 00:07:59,378
I just got out of one, remember?

132
00:08:01,839 --> 00:08:02,789
Right.

133
00:08:03,216 --> 00:08:04,467
That's right, my son.

134
00:08:05,009 --> 00:08:08,721
Why don't you just stick with your plan

135
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:11,557
to study while working in Australia?

136
00:08:13,476 --> 00:08:14,936
That's really the plan, Pops.

137
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,693
I just need to work on the paperwork.

138
00:08:28,533 --> 00:08:30,451
Bogart told me that...

139
00:08:31,536 --> 00:08:34,163
he'll also start writing in this journal.

140
00:08:34,997 --> 00:08:37,500
He wants to make up
for what happened, and...

141
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:39,585
he also wants to say sorry.

142
00:08:40,378 --> 00:08:43,089
It was never really his
intention to cause a scene.

143
00:08:44,132 --> 00:08:46,342
He just wants to protect all of us.

144
00:08:46,884 --> 00:08:47,802
And all of my other personalities.

145
00:08:48,219 --> 00:08:50,680
I get where you and Bogart are coming from,

146
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:53,224
but you still need to be careful.

147
00:08:54,559 --> 00:08:55,685
That's right, sweetheart.

148
00:08:56,144 --> 00:08:57,562
Your Nanang is right.

149
00:08:58,104 --> 00:09:00,398
My dear, If you don't
learn to take control,

150
00:09:00,606 --> 00:09:03,067
you could get yourselves into trouble.

151
00:09:04,569 --> 00:09:05,611
Yes, Nong.

152
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:08,531
I really want to say thank you and...

153
00:09:09,490 --> 00:09:12,034
I also want to apologize.

154
00:09:13,119 --> 00:09:16,372
I'm sorry that I didn't tell
you guys about the painting.

155
00:09:17,081 --> 00:09:19,996
I just don't want to be a burden.

156
00:09:20,418 --> 00:09:22,712
I also don't want to bother anyone.

157
00:09:22,867 --> 00:09:23,868
Oh, please.

158
00:09:24,422 --> 00:09:26,507
Don't think of it that way.

159
00:09:26,716 --> 00:09:29,218
We are one family here,

160
00:09:29,218 --> 00:09:30,219
- okay?
- Right.

161
00:09:30,219 --> 00:09:32,487
Why do you think our street was named...

162
00:09:32,512 --> 00:09:35,890
Magkaisang Bayan Street!

163
00:09:37,018 --> 00:09:40,104
That's why, my dear, you should know
that we're on your side.

164
00:09:40,354 --> 00:09:43,024
Don't hesitate to come to us
if something's wrong, okay?

165
00:09:43,024 --> 00:09:44,609
We'll always be here for you.

166
00:09:45,276 --> 00:09:47,069
Ninang B is right, Ate.

167
00:09:47,445 --> 00:09:51,574
And never think you're a burden, because
we never thought of you that way.

168
00:09:52,783 --> 00:09:54,191
That's right.

169
00:09:54,216 --> 00:09:56,635
My daughter Adel is right, Ysa.

170
00:09:56,749 --> 00:09:58,042
We've always felt

171
00:09:58,292 --> 00:10:01,375
happy every time we help you.

172
00:10:01,375 --> 00:10:04,230
Especially when we know
that you're safe and sound.

173
00:10:05,908 --> 00:10:10,121
We are one family, Ate.
We love one another.

174
00:10:11,302 --> 00:10:13,167
I'm really grateful for all of you.

175
00:10:13,804 --> 00:10:14,847
And also...

176
00:10:16,349 --> 00:10:17,433
you're all right.

177
00:10:18,316 --> 00:10:19,609
Even me,

178
00:10:19,769 --> 00:10:22,355
I want all my personalities
to work together.

179
00:10:22,438 --> 00:10:25,858
That's why I should also learn
how to be open with everyone here.

180
00:10:26,861 --> 00:10:31,615
Ysa, thank you for all the sacrifices you
make for all of you.

181
00:10:31,986 --> 00:10:34,400
And for continuing to paint.

182
00:10:34,855 --> 00:10:36,190
Speaking of...

183
00:10:37,202 --> 00:10:39,538
The painting is still missing.

184
00:10:39,791 --> 00:10:41,125
Hello, Ms. Amara.

185
00:10:42,147 --> 00:10:44,858
I've finished the painting. I'll bring it
to you now.

186
00:10:46,417 --> 00:10:49,540
I'm really sorry, I thought
I'd miss the deadline.

187
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:51,926
No rush. You can still perfect it.

188
00:10:51,951 --> 00:10:53,620
Just update me. Bye!

189
00:10:54,178 --> 00:10:57,890
I need to give it to Ms.
Amara tomorrow night.

190
00:10:58,230 --> 00:11:01,692
I'm afraid if I don't give it to her
on time, she'll be disappointed.

191
00:11:01,936 --> 00:11:03,980
She's the only one who trusted us.

192
00:11:04,855 --> 00:11:06,524
Oh, sweetheart, don't worry.

193
00:11:06,524 --> 00:11:08,484
We're going to help you find your painting.

194
00:11:08,484 --> 00:11:10,111
- Right?
- Of course!

195
00:11:10,111 --> 00:11:11,320
- That's right, Ysa. Okay?
- Yes, that's right!

196
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:16,492
Erna and I will post on barangay
pages and community groups online.

197
00:11:16,492 --> 00:11:19,203
I'll also ask about it in the group
chats that I'm a part of.

198
00:11:19,578 --> 00:11:24,458
- I'll talk to our customers about it too.
- Yes, that's right.

199
00:11:25,334 --> 00:11:27,503
I'll also accompany
you to the barangay hall.

200
00:11:30,673 --> 00:11:32,049
Well, go on. Text everyone.

201
00:11:32,049 --> 00:11:34,927
So we can find the painting.

202
00:11:34,952 --> 00:11:37,305
Start messaging in your group chats.

203
00:11:37,305 --> 00:11:39,323
- Bruno's here, he can help.
- Yes, that's right.

204
00:11:39,348 --> 00:11:41,517
There's still no word from our neighbors.

205
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:44,729
But at least, we already
filed a police blotter.

206
00:11:45,396 --> 00:11:48,649
Then later, we'll get the CCTV footage.

207
00:11:48,983 --> 00:11:52,778
That'll help us find whoever
stole your painting.

208
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:57,116
Because of that,
let's grab some coffee first.

209
00:11:57,742 --> 00:12:00,828
You never know. The painting might
show up and join us for coffee.

210
00:12:00,828 --> 00:12:03,748
I just hope that painting turns up soon.

211
00:12:07,001 --> 00:12:08,039
Wait a minute.

212
00:12:10,254 --> 00:12:11,339
Yes? Can I help you?

213
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,258
What are you doing here?

214
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,943
This is our café.

215
00:12:15,968 --> 00:12:17,258
I'm on duty right now.

216
00:12:18,429 --> 00:12:21,015
Oh really? I've never seen you here before.

217
00:12:21,307 --> 00:12:24,310
I bet that's just your cover. You've been
following us, haven't you?

218
00:12:25,561 --> 00:12:26,688
She's here?

219
00:12:27,063 --> 00:12:28,731
What about the painting?
Have you found it yet?

220
00:12:29,392 --> 00:12:31,269
Not yet, we're still looking for it.

221
00:12:34,779 --> 00:12:35,711
Wait.

222
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,115
Could you be the one who took the painting?

223
00:12:39,450 --> 00:12:42,953
Maybe you made up those other accomplices
just to throw us off!

224
00:12:42,953 --> 00:12:43,596
Huh?

225
00:12:43,621 --> 00:12:45,039
What if it's here in your café?

226
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:47,083
- Hey, stop. You're trespassing.
- Hey, wait a minute.

227
00:12:47,083 --> 00:12:49,377
Hey, schoolmate, you're not allowed here.

228
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:50,586
You guys know each other?

229
00:12:50,586 --> 00:12:51,562
You know me?

230
00:12:51,587 --> 00:12:52,922
Bro, she's my school mate.

231
00:12:53,482 --> 00:12:54,851
Are you looking for me?

232
00:12:55,473 --> 00:12:56,516
Keep dreaming.

233
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,178
Let me through!
I just want to see!

234
00:12:59,178 --> 00:13:01,680
- It's not here, okay?
- Let me look!

235
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,711
Stop, or we'll take this to the barangay.

236
00:13:03,933 --> 00:13:05,726
You're not allowed here.

237
00:13:05,726 --> 00:13:07,520
You're not allowed here.

238
00:13:08,312 --> 00:13:12,983
Hi Ysabelle, Just a reminder
for the painting delivery tonight.

239
00:13:13,317 --> 00:13:16,028
Looking forward to seeing it.

240
00:13:19,490 --> 00:13:21,742
- Just let me through, okay? I just need to look.
- School mate, you're really not allowed here.

241
00:13:21,742 --> 00:13:23,672
What you're doing is trespassing.

242
00:13:31,210 --> 00:13:32,878
You're not allowed there!

243
00:13:32,878 --> 00:13:33,963
Just one look!

244
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:35,443
My dear.

245
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:39,677
I heard you. I know what you're thinking.

246
00:13:41,266 --> 00:13:42,350
Lola Iska.

247
00:13:42,763 --> 00:13:45,182
My dear, I know what you're thinking.

248
00:13:45,224 --> 00:13:46,102
Ysa?

249
00:13:47,852 --> 00:13:48,758
Lola Iska!

250
00:13:49,937 --> 00:13:53,232
If you're suspicious of this guy, Adel,

251
00:13:53,441 --> 00:13:57,069
then bring him along as
we look for the painting.

252
00:13:57,653 --> 00:13:58,696
No, Lola.

253
00:13:59,071 --> 00:14:00,321
Let's look for it ourselves.

254
00:14:01,031 --> 00:14:01,977
Lola?

255
00:14:02,533 --> 00:14:03,576
Dear...

256
00:14:04,535 --> 00:14:07,371
The more eyes we have,

257
00:14:08,076 --> 00:14:11,330
the sooner we'll find what's missing.

258
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,337
That's true.

259
00:14:15,838 --> 00:14:18,591
But we're still on duty right now, Ysa.

260
00:14:19,592 --> 00:14:20,468
It's Lola Iska.

261
00:14:20,468 --> 00:14:21,430
Lola?

262
00:14:22,845 --> 00:14:23,727
Lola...

263
00:14:23,846 --> 00:14:24,735
Lola?

264
00:14:25,639 --> 00:14:26,602
Lola?

265
00:14:27,516 --> 00:14:28,809
Lola?

266
00:14:29,018 --> 00:14:30,060
Lola Iska?

267
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:37,193
Dear.

268
00:14:37,568 --> 00:14:38,375
Uh—

269
00:14:38,486 --> 00:14:41,989
Come, give me a hand.
Help me look for the painting.

270
00:14:42,490 --> 00:14:44,867
- Bro, you've got this, okay?
- Alright.

271
00:14:45,743 --> 00:14:49,330
Lola. Alright, now, listen to me. I'll tell
you everything that happened, okay?

272
00:14:49,747 --> 00:14:51,916
The mugger and I were walking here.

273
00:14:52,082 --> 00:14:53,542
We were walking happily.

274
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:55,586
Then he suddenly said "this is a holdup."

275
00:14:55,753 --> 00:14:56,754
So I got scared.

276
00:14:56,962 --> 00:14:59,256
I told him "Why are you robbing me,
I thought we were friends?"

277
00:14:59,298 --> 00:15:00,591
Then, he took my wallet.

278
00:15:00,674 --> 00:15:02,927
Then I tried to snatch it back, so we were
scrambling like this.

279
00:15:03,135 --> 00:15:05,221
And then, he suddenly
kicked me like this—bam!

280
00:15:05,596 --> 00:15:07,848
Bam! I fell right here. But he didn't...

281
00:15:08,349 --> 00:15:09,533
He didn't stop there.

282
00:15:09,558 --> 00:15:12,102
Then, he continued to beat me up.

283
00:15:12,102 --> 00:15:13,771
Pak! Pak! Pak! Pak! Pak!

284
00:15:13,979 --> 00:15:15,439
Then I was like, Pak! Pak! Pak! Pak!

285
00:15:15,439 --> 00:15:17,733
Can you stop?
You're really gonna get it.

286
00:15:19,235 --> 00:15:20,319
Tell her, not me.

287
00:15:20,736 --> 00:15:22,905
My verdict is...

288
00:15:25,866 --> 00:15:28,077
He's telling the truth, my dear.

289
00:15:28,202 --> 00:15:29,125
See?

290
00:15:29,397 --> 00:15:32,567
Because everything he said is consistent

291
00:15:32,665 --> 00:15:35,543
with what Bogart wrote in the journal.

292
00:15:35,543 --> 00:15:37,419
He finally wrote an entry on the journal.

293
00:15:38,671 --> 00:15:41,215
That doesn't help us a lot, Lola Iska.

294
00:15:41,757 --> 00:15:45,094
How can we really prove
that this guy is innocent?

295
00:15:45,719 --> 00:15:50,140
That's what I've been saying. That's why...

296
00:15:50,808 --> 00:15:54,270
we need to have the CCTV footage.

297
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:59,191
We have to see it.

298
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:00,442
Okay?

299
00:16:00,818 --> 00:16:02,403
Come on.

300
00:16:05,239 --> 00:16:07,616
Don't follow or get close
to Ate Ysa anymore.

301
00:16:07,908 --> 00:16:09,118
She might get worse again!

302
00:16:09,118 --> 00:16:12,079
If Bogart comes out, I won't be able to
stop or calm him down.

303
00:16:26,844 --> 00:16:27,866
Love?

304
00:16:29,221 --> 00:16:30,647
It's only a one-kilo order.

305
00:16:31,098 --> 00:16:33,325
Why are you preparing
enough for a feeding program?

306
00:16:33,350 --> 00:16:34,602
Sorry, my bad.

307
00:16:34,602 --> 00:16:35,603
Just let me do it.

308
00:16:37,479 --> 00:16:38,205
That's it.

309
00:16:38,230 --> 00:16:39,795
You ordered just one kilo, right?

310
00:16:40,691 --> 00:16:41,655
Here's the payment.

311
00:16:41,859 --> 00:16:42,905
Thank you.

312
00:16:43,027 --> 00:16:43,897
Alright.

313
00:16:52,202 --> 00:16:54,371
I'm just worried about Ysa.

314
00:16:54,872 --> 00:16:55,897
You know it feels like...

315
00:16:56,081 --> 00:16:58,208
they're all reverting
to how they used to be.

316
00:16:58,626 --> 00:17:00,669
She gets triggered so easily again.

317
00:17:01,170 --> 00:17:03,589
You know, it's really that man's fault.

318
00:17:04,506 --> 00:17:05,482
I told you.

319
00:17:05,623 --> 00:17:08,001
We're not supposed to mention
that man's name.

320
00:17:08,469 --> 00:17:11,013
Especially here in our house.
It's a house rule.

321
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,615
His name is Lorenz.

322
00:17:13,891 --> 00:17:16,268
You can't blame Ysabelle.

323
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,376
We taught her how to love.

324
00:17:19,698 --> 00:17:21,033
And how to be kind.

325
00:17:21,482 --> 00:17:23,067
That's the problem.

326
00:17:23,233 --> 00:17:26,028
Ysabelle has always been so obedient.

327
00:17:26,695 --> 00:17:27,780
She obeyed us.

328
00:17:28,572 --> 00:17:29,406
She loved us.

329
00:17:29,990 --> 00:17:31,168
But she also got scared.

330
00:17:31,533 --> 00:17:32,980
She ended up distancing herself.

331
00:17:33,243 --> 00:17:34,787
That's just it.

332
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:36,639
But then, Lorenz...

333
00:17:36,664 --> 00:17:37,748
gave up right away.

334
00:17:38,624 --> 00:17:40,066
We never heard from him again.

335
00:17:43,337 --> 00:17:44,457
You know, love...

336
00:17:45,798 --> 00:17:47,466
I still hope that

337
00:17:47,925 --> 00:17:50,094
one day, Ysa will meet

338
00:17:51,053 --> 00:17:52,971
a man who'll love her completely.

339
00:17:54,014 --> 00:17:55,182
Someone who will not give up on her.

340
00:17:55,516 --> 00:17:56,379
As for me...

341
00:17:56,934 --> 00:17:58,227
I don't want to trust anyone anymore.

342
00:17:59,019 --> 00:18:01,918
I don't want to see our
daughter get hurt again.

343
00:18:01,943 --> 00:18:04,571
Especially after she almost hurt herself.

344
00:18:09,989 --> 00:18:11,073
Oh, hey, Barbs!

345
00:18:11,156 --> 00:18:12,074
I'll get my order of Denurado rice—

346
00:18:12,074 --> 00:18:12,966
Girl!

347
00:18:12,991 --> 00:18:13,701
- Oh right.
- The Denurado rice.

348
00:18:13,701 --> 00:18:15,052
Yes. Denurado rice.

349
00:18:15,077 --> 00:18:16,453
One kilo, right?

350
00:18:16,453 --> 00:18:17,705
Thank you.

351
00:18:17,705 --> 00:18:18,832
Come back next time, okay?

352
00:18:18,987 --> 00:18:20,253
Alright, take care!

353
00:18:23,506 --> 00:18:24,582
You okay?

354
00:18:26,255 --> 00:18:27,261
No.

355
00:18:39,143 --> 00:18:40,519
Who is she this time, bro?

356
00:18:42,396 --> 00:18:43,597
Lola Iska.

357
00:18:45,107 --> 00:18:47,410
The fifth personality I've met.

358
00:18:49,570 --> 00:18:50,433
Lola?

359
00:18:50,779 --> 00:18:53,741
What? Like older than me?

360
00:18:56,034 --> 00:18:57,058
Something like that, Pops.

361
00:18:57,244 --> 00:18:59,363
Only in the way she thinks and acts.

362
00:19:02,207 --> 00:19:05,919
Estong, didn't you say
her painting was missing?

363
00:19:06,795 --> 00:19:09,006
Why don't you help her find the painting?

364
00:19:09,715 --> 00:19:10,924
I feel sorry for her.

365
00:19:12,134 --> 00:19:14,636
And remember, she also saved you.

366
00:19:16,972 --> 00:19:17,877
Pops...

367
00:19:18,515 --> 00:19:19,600
I already offered my help.

368
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:21,477
She doesn't want it.

369
00:19:22,269 --> 00:19:24,815
Then that girl who was
with her also said

370
00:19:25,606 --> 00:19:27,323
I might trigger her even more.

371
00:19:29,067 --> 00:19:30,049
Nah, bro.

372
00:19:30,319 --> 00:19:32,070
Popsy is right. Just help her out.

373
00:19:32,696 --> 00:19:35,282
Also, wasn't Ysa the one
who didn't want help?

374
00:19:35,657 --> 00:19:37,760
She's different now. She's a grandma.

375
00:19:41,705 --> 00:19:42,737
What about that girl?

376
00:19:45,042 --> 00:19:45,791
Bro...

377
00:19:45,834 --> 00:19:46,919
I'll take care of it.

378
00:19:47,377 --> 00:19:48,252
The girl?

379
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:49,627
That's easy.

380
00:19:53,258 --> 00:19:54,205
Watch.

381
00:19:57,638 --> 00:19:58,889
Hey, gorgeous!

382
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:04,645
Just order whatever you want. It's on me.

383
00:20:05,979 --> 00:20:07,147
I can pay for it.

384
00:20:08,315 --> 00:20:09,983
Besides, who do you think you are?

385
00:20:09,983 --> 00:20:11,276
We're not even friends.

386
00:20:11,672 --> 00:20:13,830
I mean, we can be friends.

387
00:20:14,196 --> 00:20:16,565
Pass. I have enough friends already.

388
00:20:16,865 --> 00:20:19,846
And your flattery won't work on me.
You're not my type.

389
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:20,838
Oh, my.

390
00:20:24,706 --> 00:20:25,635
Excuse me.

391
00:20:25,999 --> 00:20:26,815
Oops!

392
00:20:26,917 --> 00:20:27,501
Oh, no!

393
00:20:27,501 --> 00:20:29,294
- What the heck?!
- I'm so sorry!

394
00:20:29,795 --> 00:20:31,174
I didn't mean to.

395
00:20:31,505 --> 00:20:32,840
You're so annoying!

396
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,899
I'm so sorry.

397
00:20:33,924 --> 00:20:35,676
Gosh! Where's the
restroom? You're so annoying.

398
00:20:35,676 --> 00:20:36,860
The restroom?

399
00:20:36,885 --> 00:20:38,554
- You're so annoying!
- The restroom?

400
00:20:39,388 --> 00:20:40,643
Right over there.

401
00:20:40,806 --> 00:20:42,516
Three hundred meters, turn...

402
00:20:42,516 --> 00:20:43,100
turn around.

403
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,117
You're frustrating!

404
00:20:44,142 --> 00:20:45,435
- So annoying!
- Just go straight.

405
00:20:45,811 --> 00:20:46,807
Yes, right there.

406
00:20:47,312 --> 00:20:48,268
Sorry.

407
00:20:52,985 --> 00:20:54,319
What have I told you?

408
00:20:55,154 --> 00:20:56,307
That's your chance, bro.

409
00:20:56,868 --> 00:20:57,767
Thank you, bro.

410
00:21:00,242 --> 00:21:01,577
Lola Iska!

411
00:21:15,693 --> 00:21:18,150
Wow! You really got his face right, Lola!

412
00:21:18,176 --> 00:21:19,198
He really looked like this!

413
00:21:20,431 --> 00:21:25,127
I just based it on what Bogart
wrote in his journal.

414
00:21:26,268 --> 00:21:30,272
The best thing to do
is find this person first.

415
00:21:30,939 --> 00:21:31,899
While we...

416
00:21:32,691 --> 00:21:35,152
still don't have the CCTV footage.

417
00:21:35,944 --> 00:21:36,837
You're right, Lola.

418
00:21:36,862 --> 00:21:38,113
Let's find him first.

419
00:21:38,906 --> 00:21:40,157
Ouch.

420
00:21:43,706 --> 00:21:44,541
Lola?

421
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:45,954
You want me to...

422
00:21:46,413 --> 00:21:47,276
carry you?

423
00:21:48,707 --> 00:21:50,125
Oh, no need!

424
00:21:51,126 --> 00:21:52,377
I can manage.

425
00:21:52,377 --> 00:21:54,945
I might end up aching even more.

426
00:22:00,764 --> 00:22:03,684
I think you're the one
who's getting tired, dear.

427
00:22:04,512 --> 00:22:06,514
Do you want to take a rest for a while?

428
00:22:08,477 --> 00:22:09,661
Just a little bit.

429
00:22:09,686 --> 00:22:10,746
Is it okay with you?

430
00:22:10,771 --> 00:22:11,750
Let's rest for a while?

431
00:22:12,397 --> 00:22:14,316
But you're still so young.

432
00:22:15,192 --> 00:22:16,007
But...

433
00:22:16,510 --> 00:22:17,546
Alright.

434
00:22:18,111 --> 00:22:19,734
But just for a short while, okay?

435
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,950
We might run out of time.

436
00:22:23,283 --> 00:22:24,273
Okay, Lola.

437
00:22:24,618 --> 00:22:26,171
Then, we'll start looking again.

438
00:22:39,508 --> 00:22:41,301
Wow, it's so accurate.

439
00:22:45,389 --> 00:22:47,808
You even got his beard right.

440
00:22:54,606 --> 00:22:55,557
This is impressive.

441
00:22:57,085 --> 00:22:58,127
Even his eyes.

442
00:22:59,611 --> 00:23:02,656
Yay! Play! Play! Play!

443
00:23:03,115 --> 00:23:04,033
Lola?

444
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:07,052
I'll join! Let me join!

445
00:23:07,077 --> 00:23:08,845
Why do you talk like that?

446
00:23:08,870 --> 00:23:10,664
You're a grown-up!

447
00:23:10,856 --> 00:23:12,900
Do you even know what we're playing?

448
00:23:13,166 --> 00:23:14,432
Pass! You don't have a clue!

449
00:23:14,459 --> 00:23:15,961
Let's get out of here!

450
00:23:16,003 --> 00:23:19,965
I want to play! Yeye wants to play!

451
00:23:19,965 --> 00:23:22,268
Kuya, your girlfriend is crazy!

452
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:25,971
Come on, let's go!

453
00:23:26,638 --> 00:23:28,041
Want to play with me instead?

454
00:23:28,557 --> 00:23:29,588
Come, let's play!

455
00:23:29,613 --> 00:23:31,065
I'll play with you instead.

456
00:23:33,186 --> 00:23:34,104
Let's play?

457
00:23:35,031 --> 00:23:36,241
Kuya Estong?

458
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,627
You remember me?

459
00:23:40,527 --> 00:23:42,946
Thank you!

460
00:23:42,946 --> 00:23:43,893
Balloon!

461
00:23:45,615 --> 00:23:46,518
Yes!

462
00:23:46,742 --> 00:23:48,994
Let's play, just the two of us!

463
00:23:48,994 --> 00:23:49,761
Let's play?

464
00:23:49,786 --> 00:23:50,637
Of course!

465
00:23:50,662 --> 00:23:52,330
Let's play!

466
00:23:58,795 --> 00:24:00,221
I'll go first, okay?

467
00:24:02,591 --> 00:24:05,093
- That's cheating!
- Nope, nope, nope!

468
00:24:05,118 --> 00:24:06,870
You're a cheater!

469
00:24:08,298 --> 00:24:09,800
So close!

470
00:24:11,391 --> 00:24:12,517
You lost!

471
00:24:12,517 --> 00:24:13,346
Your turn.

472
00:24:13,846 --> 00:24:16,348
I'll lose it you'll get through that, okay?

473
00:24:20,067 --> 00:24:20,916
Come on, then.

474
00:24:20,941 --> 00:24:22,565
Wow, you're quick!

475
00:24:24,154 --> 00:24:27,491
- Wow, you're so good!
- I won!

476
00:24:29,993 --> 00:24:30,786
Alright, here.

477
00:24:30,827 --> 00:24:31,752
Congrats, Yeye!

478
00:24:33,413 --> 00:24:36,229
You're so good, Yeye. You got me there!

479
00:24:37,250 --> 00:24:38,126
Kuya Estong?

480
00:24:38,668 --> 00:24:39,900
Yes? What is it, Yeye?

481
00:24:40,837 --> 00:24:42,005
Are we best friends now?

482
00:24:43,423 --> 00:24:45,008
Sure! We're best friends now!

483
00:24:45,175 --> 00:24:46,151
Pinky swear?

484
00:24:46,176 --> 00:24:47,177
Pinky swear!

485
00:24:48,208 --> 00:24:50,119
We're now best friends, okay?

486
00:24:51,056 --> 00:24:53,225
So now that we're best friends...

487
00:24:53,892 --> 00:24:56,686
Maybe you could help
me find Ate Ysa's painting.

488
00:24:57,312 --> 00:24:58,291
- Okay?
- Yes!

489
00:24:59,022 --> 00:24:59,877
Let's go?

490
00:25:02,361 --> 00:25:05,253
Go faster, best friend!

491
00:25:05,278 --> 00:25:06,863
Yeye, you're so fast!

492
00:25:07,781 --> 00:25:09,032
We're so sorry.

493
00:25:09,658 --> 00:25:10,592
Sorry.

494
00:25:10,617 --> 00:25:11,743
Are you okay, Yeye?

495
00:25:16,706 --> 00:25:17,666
Yeye?

496
00:25:24,297 --> 00:25:27,717
O to the M to the G!

497
00:25:27,717 --> 00:25:29,803
To the H to the I!

498
00:25:29,803 --> 00:25:31,113
Oh my god.

499
00:25:31,138 --> 00:25:31,972
The designs are so pretty!

500
00:25:31,998 --> 00:25:33,031
This one!

501
00:25:33,056 --> 00:25:35,142
Oh, I like this!

502
00:25:35,142 --> 00:25:37,619
Oh my God!

503
00:25:37,644 --> 00:25:39,229
This is so nice!

504
00:25:39,271 --> 00:25:40,580
Oh my God, wait a minute.

505
00:25:40,605 --> 00:25:42,190
I think this one is perfect for you.

506
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:45,752
The color, the shape,
the flowery design. And...

507
00:25:45,777 --> 00:25:48,157
It matches with your hair color. Perfect!

508
00:25:48,182 --> 00:25:49,781
I know. Yeah!

509
00:25:49,781 --> 00:25:50,323
Right?

510
00:25:50,323 --> 00:25:50,966
Wait.

511
00:25:50,991 --> 00:25:51,867
Yes?

512
00:25:51,867 --> 00:25:53,034
No offense, but...

513
00:25:53,034 --> 00:25:53,660
Mhmm.

514
00:25:53,743 --> 00:25:54,807
Are you gay?

515
00:25:57,581 --> 00:25:58,290
No!

516
00:25:58,290 --> 00:26:01,560
But you know, I've always been
a fan of fashion! Right?

517
00:26:01,585 --> 00:26:02,794
Fashion!

518
00:26:03,253 --> 00:26:04,671
Fashion!

519
00:26:04,696 --> 00:26:10,002
I know you. You're the one
I saw at Ukay Orayt.

520
00:26:12,137 --> 00:26:12,762
Right?

521
00:26:12,762 --> 00:26:14,181
You're right!

522
00:26:14,222 --> 00:26:16,391
Alright, I know!

523
00:26:16,391 --> 00:26:18,018
Why are you always with me?

524
00:26:18,143 --> 00:26:19,603
Are you my admirer?

525
00:26:19,811 --> 00:26:21,236
Do you have a crush on me?

526
00:26:21,410 --> 00:26:23,662
How did you know I'm your admirer?

527
00:26:24,149 --> 00:26:26,276
Yes, that's right! Because you know

528
00:26:26,318 --> 00:26:28,653
your fashion sense is really top-notch!

529
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:30,229
Top-notch!

530
00:26:30,254 --> 00:26:34,009
Then you should sign up to my fan club!

531
00:26:34,034 --> 00:26:35,869
And then I'll welcome you!

532
00:26:35,869 --> 00:26:36,578
You'll welcome me?

533
00:26:36,578 --> 00:26:37,537
Yeah!

534
00:26:37,537 --> 00:26:39,539
Oh and then welcome to me— to Cacainatics?

535
00:26:40,459 --> 00:26:41,541
Well, that'll do.

536
00:26:42,609 --> 00:26:43,518
I love it!

537
00:26:43,543 --> 00:26:45,712
Look, this one's perfect!

538
00:26:45,712 --> 00:26:46,421
It's a hundred and two pesos, mister.

539
00:26:46,421 --> 00:26:47,672
- One hundred and twenty pesos?
- Yes, mister

540
00:26:47,672 --> 00:26:49,299
Can I put it in my bag already?

541
00:26:49,324 --> 00:26:50,258
- It's so expensive.
- Okay.

542
00:26:50,300 --> 00:26:52,427
I'll get this and I'll get four of these.

543
00:26:52,427 --> 00:26:53,094
Same price for this?

544
00:26:53,136 --> 00:26:53,924
- And then...
- Yes, mister.

545
00:26:53,949 --> 00:26:56,431
Oh, their colors are
nice! Which one is better?

546
00:26:56,431 --> 00:26:58,158
- Are you the one paying for these?
- Yes, ma'am. That looks nice.

547
00:26:58,183 --> 00:26:59,059
Oh, I choose this one!

548
00:26:59,059 --> 00:27:00,619
Hey, those cost one
hundred twenty pesos each.

549
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:07,311
- Ate Ysa, where are you now.
- Hello, hello, Kuya?

550
00:27:08,693 --> 00:27:10,182
Hello? Hello?

551
00:27:15,784 --> 00:27:16,775
Hello? Kuya!

552
00:27:17,661 --> 00:27:18,803
Kuya? Kuya?

553
00:27:18,828 --> 00:27:21,206
Oh, kuya, I'm glad you picked up.
Where are you?

554
00:27:21,331 --> 00:27:22,874
I'm here right behind you.

555
00:27:22,958 --> 00:27:23,767
What do you mean "behind you"?

556
00:27:23,792 --> 00:27:25,377
Kuya, you're not behind me—

557
00:27:26,169 --> 00:27:27,197
It's just me.

558
00:27:27,337 --> 00:27:30,166
How could he answer you when he left
his phone here?

559
00:27:32,092 --> 00:27:33,041
Oh, come on.

560
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:34,119
Seriously?

561
00:27:35,595 --> 00:27:37,033
I was calling him this whole time.

562
00:27:38,723 --> 00:27:40,127
This is your fault!

563
00:27:40,517 --> 00:27:43,353
You think I didn't know you
intentionally threw the water at me?!

564
00:27:43,472 --> 00:27:45,057
Hold on, how can you say that?

565
00:27:45,397 --> 00:27:46,564
Your style sucks!

566
00:27:46,982 --> 00:27:47,854
It's awful!

567
00:27:48,525 --> 00:27:49,459
Um...

568
00:27:49,484 --> 00:27:50,197
Miss?

569
00:27:50,944 --> 00:27:53,150
Sorry about my youngest.

570
00:27:53,363 --> 00:27:55,532
He meant no harm.

571
00:27:56,241 --> 00:27:57,377
Yeah, that's right.

572
00:27:57,409 --> 00:27:59,869
My brother just wants to help your Ate Ysa.

573
00:28:00,252 --> 00:28:01,721
You're just really annoying!

574
00:28:01,746 --> 00:28:03,748
What if your brother
will trigger her again?!

575
00:28:04,165 --> 00:28:05,500
It's always your brother!

576
00:28:06,376 --> 00:28:07,627
Don't worry.

577
00:28:08,118 --> 00:28:11,538
Estong wouldn't just abandon Ysa.

578
00:28:11,715 --> 00:28:15,427
Actually, last night we saw him researching

579
00:28:15,552 --> 00:28:17,178
how to interact

580
00:28:17,762 --> 00:28:18,972
with people like Ysa.

581
00:28:19,681 --> 00:28:20,479
Right!

582
00:28:20,849 --> 00:28:22,809
So don't underestimate my brother, okay?

583
00:28:23,143 --> 00:28:25,395
He may look like a fool
compared to me, but...

584
00:28:25,854 --> 00:28:27,247
he's got his own strengths too.

585
00:28:27,272 --> 00:28:29,107
Especially if she likes the girl.

586
00:28:31,526 --> 00:28:32,385
What?

587
00:28:32,902 --> 00:28:34,213
Does he have a crush on Ate Ysa?

588
00:28:35,206 --> 00:28:37,041
No! That can't happen!

589
00:28:37,407 --> 00:28:38,508
What do you mean, that can't happen?

590
00:28:38,626 --> 00:28:40,461
What do you want? That my brother
has a crush on you instead?

591
00:28:40,994 --> 00:28:44,289
You don't understand! It's a long story,
but it can't happen!

592
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,033
Ate Belle might come out!

593
00:28:46,708 --> 00:28:47,682
Ate Belle?

594
00:28:48,251 --> 00:28:49,102
Wait, so...

595
00:28:49,127 --> 00:28:50,962
That's her sixth personality?

596
00:28:51,713 --> 00:28:53,273
That's how scary she is?

597
00:28:53,298 --> 00:28:54,291
Yes!

598
00:28:54,549 --> 00:28:56,217
If Ate Belle really comes out,

599
00:28:56,217 --> 00:28:57,469
she'll definitely put
your brother in danger!

600
00:28:57,594 --> 00:28:58,924
He'll have nowhere to run!

601
00:29:02,098 --> 00:29:02,979
Jayden.

602
00:29:03,224 --> 00:29:04,784
You should just accompany Adel.

603
00:29:04,932 --> 00:29:06,436
You have a motorcycle, right?

604
00:29:06,519 --> 00:29:08,438
That way, you'll find them both faster.

605
00:29:09,105 --> 00:29:10,273
Okay, Popsy. You're right.

606
00:29:10,482 --> 00:29:11,941
Come on, let's get going!

607
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:13,376
Hey!

608
00:29:13,401 --> 00:29:15,570
Don't be so fussy. They
could be fighting already!

609
00:29:15,570 --> 00:29:17,611
They might've already hurt each other.
Come on.

610
00:29:18,490 --> 00:29:19,471
Come on.

611
00:30:04,619 --> 00:30:07,122
Okay, that's perfect.

612
00:30:07,122 --> 00:30:07,622
And then—

613
00:30:07,622 --> 00:30:08,991
What if I'll place this hand, so I can—

614
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:10,016
Yeah!

615
00:30:10,041 --> 00:30:11,768
That's right. Okay and then...

616
00:30:11,793 --> 00:30:15,171
Try tilting your face a
bit to the right. Okay?

617
00:30:15,171 --> 00:30:16,022
Like this?

618
00:30:16,047 --> 00:30:18,591
Yes! Oh my God, that's the angle!

619
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:19,300
Woo!

620
00:30:19,342 --> 00:30:20,195
Mhmm!

621
00:30:20,385 --> 00:30:21,148
One more.

622
00:30:34,357 --> 00:30:35,515
Jestoni!

623
00:30:36,192 --> 00:30:37,152
What's going on?

624
00:30:37,152 --> 00:30:38,778
Okay, that's it.

625
00:30:38,945 --> 00:30:39,571
It's done!

626
00:30:39,571 --> 00:30:41,114
Oh, I wanna see!

627
00:30:41,114 --> 00:30:43,241
Let me see! Let me see!

628
00:30:43,867 --> 00:30:44,734
Look!

629
00:30:45,076 --> 00:30:46,494
- Right?
- It's so nice!

630
00:30:46,494 --> 00:30:47,704
I know!

631
00:30:48,079 --> 00:30:49,247
I look like a star there!

632
00:30:49,247 --> 00:30:49,831
I look like a star there!

633
00:30:49,831 --> 00:30:52,542
- Yeah!
- I look like an artist!

634
00:30:52,542 --> 00:30:54,109
I know, right? Clock it!

635
00:30:55,211 --> 00:30:56,629
It's so nice!

636
00:30:56,963 --> 00:30:59,640
Oh! My legs are so long!

637
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:01,273
Yeah...

638
00:31:02,510 --> 00:31:03,845
Can we just stick with...

639
00:31:03,970 --> 00:31:04,804
just Estong?

640
00:31:04,874 --> 00:31:06,960
I'm not used to being called Jestoni.

641
00:31:07,765 --> 00:31:08,283
No.

642
00:31:08,308 --> 00:31:09,767
No, no, no.

643
00:31:09,792 --> 00:31:10,835
You know why?

644
00:31:11,311 --> 00:31:12,624
Because Estong...

645
00:31:13,813 --> 00:31:14,570
Why?

646
00:31:14,772 --> 00:31:17,650
Kinda sounds lame.

647
00:31:17,775 --> 00:31:18,902
And I don't like—

648
00:31:19,068 --> 00:31:21,898
I like all things pretty, you know?

649
00:31:22,155 --> 00:31:23,698
That's why I'll call you Jestoni.

650
00:31:24,282 --> 00:31:27,911
There's Estong, but Jestoni! Right?

651
00:31:28,661 --> 00:31:29,996
Right!

652
00:31:29,996 --> 00:31:31,831
Yeah, it came from Jestoni.

653
00:31:31,831 --> 00:31:33,374
Yeah! Jestoni!

654
00:31:33,374 --> 00:31:34,601
So, you're good?

655
00:31:34,626 --> 00:31:37,587
So can we now head to the barangay hall

656
00:31:37,587 --> 00:31:41,007
to get the CCTV footage for the painting?

657
00:31:41,716 --> 00:31:42,525
Remember?

658
00:31:42,550 --> 00:31:45,737
O to the M to the G!

659
00:31:45,762 --> 00:31:49,460
Why didn't you remind
me? I completely forgot!

660
00:31:50,058 --> 00:31:51,601
We have to look for that painting.

661
00:31:51,601 --> 00:31:52,852
We have to get it.

662
00:31:52,852 --> 00:31:53,140
Yes!

663
00:31:53,165 --> 00:31:56,873
Because the whole world
has to see my beautiful artwork!

664
00:31:56,898 --> 00:31:58,733
Yes! I know!

665
00:31:58,733 --> 00:32:00,860
We have to get it. We
have to look for it, okay?

666
00:32:00,860 --> 00:32:02,278
I did everything I could for her!

667
00:32:02,278 --> 00:32:06,324
I even did her laundry,
yet she still left me!

668
00:32:08,535 --> 00:32:09,219
So...

669
00:32:09,244 --> 00:32:11,079
Let's go! Let's go now!

670
00:32:11,955 --> 00:32:12,562
Cacai?

671
00:32:13,915 --> 00:32:14,656
Cacai?

672
00:32:26,177 --> 00:32:28,054
Have I been with you
this whole time, Estong?

673
00:32:31,808 --> 00:32:32,757
Tristan?

674
00:32:33,685 --> 00:32:35,311
Uh— yes. We need to go somewhere.

675
00:32:37,063 --> 00:32:38,106
I don't want to go.

676
00:32:39,649 --> 00:32:40,608
I'm too sad at the moment.

677
00:32:42,902 --> 00:32:43,903
Oh.

678
00:32:44,866 --> 00:32:45,922
Alright.

679
00:32:45,947 --> 00:32:49,284
Let's just take a walk.
Let's walk while being sad.

680
00:32:50,201 --> 00:32:51,202
I don't to walk either.

681
00:32:53,830 --> 00:32:54,747
What do you wanna do?

682
00:33:28,239 --> 00:33:30,116
Whoa! One hundred!

683
00:33:32,035 --> 00:33:33,411
So good! Your turn.

684
00:33:35,997 --> 00:33:37,031
I don't want to.

685
00:33:38,541 --> 00:33:39,375
You go ahead, bro.

686
00:33:43,379 --> 00:33:44,714
Tristan. If...

687
00:33:45,340 --> 00:33:47,091
you're not going to sing with me,

688
00:33:48,217 --> 00:33:50,970
maybe you could come with me to help
look for Ysa's painting.

689
00:33:51,554 --> 00:33:52,335
What do you think?

690
00:34:00,271 --> 00:34:01,140
I don't want to.

691
00:34:05,234 --> 00:34:07,070
They're the only ones who want to find it.

692
00:34:09,030 --> 00:34:12,843
They're the only ones who wanted to be
recognized because of that painting.

693
00:34:20,416 --> 00:34:21,335
How about you?

694
00:34:21,626 --> 00:34:22,585
What do you want?

695
00:34:29,884 --> 00:34:31,469
I just want to be happy.

696
00:34:41,813 --> 00:34:42,939
How about you?

697
00:34:48,277 --> 00:34:49,696
I want to...

698
00:34:52,657 --> 00:34:54,033
Your question's too difficult to answer.

699
00:34:55,785 --> 00:34:56,911
The truth is...

700
00:34:57,620 --> 00:34:58,538
I don't know.

701
00:34:59,998 --> 00:35:02,673
I don't know if I'll ever find out.

702
00:35:07,296 --> 00:35:08,589
You said it yourself,

703
00:35:10,466 --> 00:35:12,093
"Think positive."

704
00:35:15,012 --> 00:35:16,848
What was it your father used to say again?

705
00:35:19,767 --> 00:35:21,269
While there's still breath in us...

706
00:35:22,019 --> 00:35:23,087
there's still a fight in us.

707
00:35:35,657 --> 00:35:36,548
Are you okay?

708
00:35:43,958 --> 00:35:44,704
Hey are you okay?

709
00:35:44,917 --> 00:35:45,743
Tristan?

710
00:35:46,002 --> 00:35:46,775
Tristan?

711
00:35:51,632 --> 00:35:52,470
Are you okay?

712
00:35:53,009 --> 00:35:54,026
What happened?

713
00:35:54,051 --> 00:35:56,888
Ugh... my neck's starting to hurt.

714
00:36:01,017 --> 00:36:01,939
Oh no!

715
00:36:02,351 --> 00:36:03,282
Hey! Oh God!

716
00:36:03,603 --> 00:36:04,287
She lost—

717
00:36:04,312 --> 00:36:05,146
Lola Iska?

718
00:36:06,439 --> 00:36:08,149
Lola— Lola is passing out!

719
00:36:08,149 --> 00:36:08,858
Here, here.

720
00:36:08,858 --> 00:36:09,442
It's okay.

721
00:36:09,484 --> 00:36:09,817
Lola?

722
00:36:09,817 --> 00:36:13,905
Ugh, my neck's killing me.
What did those kids eat?

723
00:36:15,239 --> 00:36:16,267
Pork rinds and beer.

724
00:36:17,074 --> 00:36:18,451
What does it say?

725
00:36:19,410 --> 00:36:21,120
She definitely drunk.

726
00:36:22,371 --> 00:36:23,623
I guess she really drunk.

727
00:36:23,956 --> 00:36:25,458
What about you?
Aren't you drunk yet?

728
00:36:25,458 --> 00:36:27,210
I'm not yet.

729
00:36:27,210 --> 00:36:30,046
What's with those kids?!

730
00:36:30,546 --> 00:36:33,299
They're going to give me a heart attack!

731
00:36:33,299 --> 00:36:35,593
- Lola, calm down.
- Oh gosh, it hurts!

732
00:36:35,593 --> 00:36:37,053
Relax, relax.

733
00:36:37,303 --> 00:36:39,472
What were those kids thinking?!

734
00:36:39,472 --> 00:36:41,641
Easy, easy. You might give yourself a
heart attack.

735
00:36:47,188 --> 00:36:48,606
Go ahead and carry it.

736
00:36:49,816 --> 00:36:50,358
Is she dead?

737
00:36:50,358 --> 00:36:51,459
She just fell asleep, okay?

738
00:36:51,484 --> 00:36:52,485
She's drunk.

739
00:36:57,114 --> 00:36:58,032
I need my medicine!

740
00:36:58,115 --> 00:36:59,826
Medicine, we need medicine!

741
00:37:07,291 --> 00:37:08,118
Lola?

742
00:37:17,176 --> 00:37:19,178
Am I getting too heavy for you, dear?

743
00:37:19,512 --> 00:37:20,905
You can put me down now.

744
00:37:20,930 --> 00:37:21,892
Not at all, Lola.

745
00:37:22,682 --> 00:37:24,725
Better than you having a heart attack.

746
00:37:25,434 --> 00:37:26,415
I got this.

747
00:37:27,603 --> 00:37:28,470
Uh, lola?

748
00:37:29,647 --> 00:37:33,359
Was it Tristan eating chicharon
that triggered you?

749
00:37:33,359 --> 00:37:35,064
Is that why your neck started hurting?

750
00:37:36,529 --> 00:37:37,204
Yeah.

751
00:37:38,614 --> 00:37:42,603
That's why I keep telling those kids...

752
00:37:43,703 --> 00:37:45,079
That they should always...

753
00:37:46,455 --> 00:37:48,416
think about the others as well.

754
00:37:48,416 --> 00:37:51,210
Because whatever they do...

755
00:37:51,961 --> 00:37:54,797
whatever they think, or feel...

756
00:37:55,381 --> 00:37:58,040
it affects everyone else too.

757
00:37:58,718 --> 00:38:01,929
That's what they need
to get through their heads.

758
00:38:06,517 --> 00:38:08,311
I didn't realize Ysa was carrying so much.

759
00:38:09,645 --> 00:38:11,063
What was that, dear? Heavy?

760
00:38:11,856 --> 00:38:14,609
- Well, you can put me down now.
- Oh, no, no. That's not what I meant.

761
00:38:14,942 --> 00:38:17,028
You can stay there as long as you want.

762
00:38:17,445 --> 00:38:18,485
No.

763
00:38:18,863 --> 00:38:20,114
It's okay, you can put me down now.

764
00:38:20,531 --> 00:38:21,509
I can manage.

765
00:38:29,665 --> 00:38:30,517
And...

766
00:38:32,460 --> 00:38:33,461
I have this.

767
00:38:39,717 --> 00:38:40,927
Oh, I almost forgot.

768
00:38:42,261 --> 00:38:43,846
You haven't properly greet your lola yet.

769
00:38:46,181 --> 00:38:46,845
Come on.

770
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:55,399
Lola?

771
00:38:56,859 --> 00:38:57,806
Lola?

772
00:38:58,027 --> 00:38:59,403
We're in the middle of the street, Lola!

773
00:39:01,072 --> 00:39:01,915
There we go.

774
00:39:02,531 --> 00:39:03,407
Where am I?

775
00:39:05,216 --> 00:39:06,217
We're just in the street.

776
00:39:08,829 --> 00:39:09,789
Let's get going, my dear.

777
00:39:14,115 --> 00:39:14,990
Dear.

778
00:39:15,127 --> 00:39:17,004
Do we still got a long way to go?

779
00:39:17,793 --> 00:39:19,878
I'm getting a little tired.

780
00:39:21,050 --> 00:39:22,301
Just a little more, Lola.

781
00:39:23,142 --> 00:39:24,477
You never know.

782
00:39:27,014 --> 00:39:30,101
Maybe the universe will
help us out, and we'll just run

783
00:39:30,643 --> 00:39:31,977
into the mugger. Right?

784
00:39:32,561 --> 00:39:33,485
That'd be awesome.

785
00:39:36,023 --> 00:39:36,884
Dear...

786
00:39:37,108 --> 00:39:37,993
Yes, Lola?

787
00:39:38,943 --> 00:39:39,902
Isn't that the mugger?

788
00:39:46,283 --> 00:39:47,306
It is!

789
00:39:47,910 --> 00:39:49,017
Hey! You!

790
00:39:53,124 --> 00:39:54,250
Come here!

791
00:39:54,291 --> 00:39:55,048
You!

792
00:39:56,585 --> 00:39:57,462
Hey!

793
00:39:59,157 --> 00:40:00,024
Hey!

794
00:40:03,592 --> 00:40:05,136
Get over here!

795
00:40:06,721 --> 00:40:07,596
Get over here!

796
00:40:07,596 --> 00:40:08,806
What? You want to run away?!

797
00:40:08,889 --> 00:40:10,384
You think you can escape now?!

798
00:40:10,725 --> 00:40:12,101
Forgive me, please!

799
00:40:13,144 --> 00:40:15,104
Why did you even bother
making us chase you?

800
00:40:15,354 --> 00:40:16,605
Why? Did anyone tell you to chase me?

801
00:40:17,273 --> 00:40:18,438
You didn't have to, right?

802
00:40:21,318 --> 00:40:22,611
So you're a smartass, huh?

803
00:40:22,611 --> 00:40:24,196
The nerve of you!

804
00:40:24,196 --> 00:40:25,698
Bogart, don't.

805
00:40:25,698 --> 00:40:27,074
You don't need to hurt him.

806
00:40:27,700 --> 00:40:29,910
You might hurt yourself and the others.

807
00:40:30,244 --> 00:40:31,181
He's right, ma'am!

808
00:40:31,370 --> 00:40:32,496
You should listen to him!

809
00:40:32,913 --> 00:40:33,998
Tell me the truth.

810
00:40:34,431 --> 00:40:36,392
You're accomplices with the guys
who stole my painting, huh?

811
00:40:36,417 --> 00:40:37,918
No! I don't have any accomplices.

812
00:40:38,419 --> 00:40:39,336
What painting?

813
00:40:43,132 --> 00:40:44,633
Are you sure about that?

814
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:45,968
I was just passing by.

815
00:40:46,385 --> 00:40:48,929
I was just doing it for my sick child.

816
00:40:49,055 --> 00:40:51,599
Just make sure you're telling the truth!

817
00:40:51,849 --> 00:40:55,603
You won't answer to the
law. You'll answer to my fists.

818
00:40:55,603 --> 00:40:56,845
Do you understand?!

819
00:40:56,979 --> 00:40:57,954
Yes, boss!

820
00:40:58,189 --> 00:40:59,565
Boss, if you want,

821
00:40:59,982 --> 00:41:01,692
you can accompany me to the hospital.

822
00:41:03,319 --> 00:41:04,403
Get out of here.

823
00:41:07,321 --> 00:41:08,886
You're really pissing me off.

824
00:41:11,535 --> 00:41:12,536
Hey, calm down.

825
00:41:15,664 --> 00:41:16,665
Don't worry.

826
00:41:17,291 --> 00:41:18,793
We'll find Ysa's painting eventually.

827
00:41:21,170 --> 00:41:22,023
It's okay, Bogart.

828
00:41:23,339 --> 00:41:24,234
Calm down.

829
00:41:41,607 --> 00:41:42,461
Estong.

830
00:41:44,641 --> 00:41:45,492
Ysa.

831
00:41:47,446 --> 00:41:48,313
Welcome back.

832
00:41:52,868 --> 00:41:54,036
- Ate Ysa.
- Oh, there they are.

833
00:41:54,805 --> 00:41:55,671
Adel?

834
00:41:59,875 --> 00:42:00,805
Bro!

835
00:42:01,669 --> 00:42:02,656
Ate Ysa!

836
00:42:02,753 --> 00:42:04,484
Are you okay? Did he hurt you?

837
00:42:05,422 --> 00:42:06,188
No.

838
00:42:06,632 --> 00:42:08,676
I was completely safe because of Estong.

839
00:42:09,385 --> 00:42:10,236
See?

840
00:42:10,261 --> 00:42:11,289
Did you hear that?

841
00:42:11,595 --> 00:42:12,555
I told you.

842
00:42:12,847 --> 00:42:14,723
Estong is really caring.

843
00:42:14,723 --> 00:42:15,224
Yes.

844
00:42:15,307 --> 00:42:17,101
He cares with all his heart.

845
00:42:17,918 --> 00:42:18,867
What are you saying, bro?

846
00:42:19,645 --> 00:42:21,689
Are you sure, Ate Ysa? Maybe you just
didn't remember.

847
00:42:23,023 --> 00:42:23,836
No.

848
00:42:24,108 --> 00:42:25,234
I saw everything.

849
00:42:25,818 --> 00:42:28,154
I remember everything because they showed
me everything.

850
00:42:32,324 --> 00:42:33,490
They showed you everything?

851
00:42:35,467 --> 00:42:36,185
How?

852
00:42:41,625 --> 00:42:43,084
The barangay hall texted me.

853
00:42:43,419 --> 00:42:45,713
They said we can check
the CCTV footage now.

854
00:43:01,604 --> 00:43:02,897
That's way too blurry.

855
00:43:04,607 --> 00:43:07,985
It caught the men who
stole Ate Ysa's painting.

856
00:43:08,736 --> 00:43:11,113
But the footage is glitching
that's why it's blurry.

857
00:43:11,113 --> 00:43:12,114
We can't see their faces.

858
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:16,162
Ysa.

859
00:43:16,952 --> 00:43:19,705
Why is that painting so important to you?

860
00:43:22,541 --> 00:43:24,210
It's important to me because...

861
00:43:26,119 --> 00:43:27,162
It's my dream.

862
00:43:27,880 --> 00:43:29,048
It's our dream.

863
00:43:31,383 --> 00:43:32,334
Oh.

864
00:43:35,763 --> 00:43:37,973
Didn't I tell you? We're not all the same.

865
00:43:40,059 --> 00:43:43,062
But that was the only way I could think of
to bring us together.

866
00:43:43,562 --> 00:43:45,397
That's also what our doctor told us.

867
00:43:45,898 --> 00:43:48,400
That even though we
have different personalities...

868
00:43:49,526 --> 00:43:51,529
it's good for us to have

869
00:43:51,737 --> 00:43:52,821
shared dreams,

870
00:43:53,197 --> 00:43:54,240
shared goals.

871
00:43:55,115 --> 00:43:56,068
Like that.

872
00:43:57,660 --> 00:43:58,702
I see.

873
00:44:02,456 --> 00:44:03,459
Estong?

874
00:44:05,526 --> 00:44:06,611
I'm sorry.

875
00:44:08,045 --> 00:44:10,714
I know today wasn't easy.

876
00:44:12,007 --> 00:44:13,904
You've been through
so much with a lot of us.

877
00:44:15,219 --> 00:44:16,545
You had to take care a lot of us.

878
00:44:17,846 --> 00:44:19,598
Sorry for bothering you.

879
00:44:21,809 --> 00:44:23,102
Um. Ysa...

880
00:44:24,770 --> 00:44:26,355
The truth is...

881
00:44:28,274 --> 00:44:29,275
I enjoyed it.

882
00:44:30,609 --> 00:44:32,060
Different personalities.

883
00:44:32,444 --> 00:44:33,412
Different vibes.

884
00:44:33,737 --> 00:44:34,474
It was fun.

885
00:44:42,467 --> 00:44:44,957
- When will I get the painting?
- Oh no.

886
00:44:45,332 --> 00:44:47,418
Ms. Amara texted me.
What am I going to do?

887
00:44:47,710 --> 00:44:49,211
She's asking about the painting.

888
00:44:52,214 --> 00:44:53,215
What if...

889
00:44:54,431 --> 00:44:56,391
You just tell her the truth, and then...

890
00:44:56,468 --> 00:44:57,928
create a new artwork.

891
00:44:58,971 --> 00:45:00,347
It's not that easy.

892
00:45:01,223 --> 00:45:02,850
Ate Ysa promised.

893
00:45:04,268 --> 00:45:07,396
She was commissioned to paint that for
Ms. Amara's house.

894
00:45:08,689 --> 00:45:10,357
He's right, you know?

895
00:45:10,941 --> 00:45:12,735
It's better to tell the truth.

896
00:45:13,444 --> 00:45:14,903
And of course,

897
00:45:15,195 --> 00:45:17,281
don't lose hope because...

898
00:45:17,990 --> 00:45:19,658
While there's still breath in us...

899
00:45:19,950 --> 00:45:21,618
There's still fight in us.

900
00:45:24,371 --> 00:45:25,581
Let's go, Ate.

901
00:45:33,380 --> 00:45:35,841
Alright, that's enough.
Let's have something to eat.

902
00:45:36,008 --> 00:45:37,634
- Come on?
- You're not coming!

903
00:45:38,635 --> 00:45:40,721
Ate Ysa, are you okay?

904
00:45:40,888 --> 00:45:43,140
- Ysa?
- I found the painting.

905
00:45:47,561 --> 00:45:49,229
You can't take this away.

906
00:45:49,646 --> 00:45:50,981
I won't return it.

907
00:45:50,981 --> 00:45:52,190
That's mine!

908
00:45:52,399 --> 00:45:53,734
Sir, that belongs to me.

909
00:45:53,734 --> 00:45:55,110
I made that myself.

910
00:45:55,135 --> 00:45:56,428
I completely understand

911
00:45:56,453 --> 00:45:58,414
if you won't give me
another chance

912
00:45:58,439 --> 00:46:00,274
or a spot for the next exhibit.

913
00:46:00,657 --> 00:46:01,325
Ysa?

914
00:46:01,325 --> 00:46:02,534
Hey! Ysa!

915
00:46:02,534 --> 00:46:04,161
- Ysa! Ysa!
- Ate? Ate!

916
00:46:04,186 --> 00:46:06,409
Sometimes, the body
decides it needs to rest.

917
00:46:06,626 --> 00:46:08,003
Like a reset, Doc?

918
00:46:08,028 --> 00:46:09,195
Something like that.

919
00:46:09,220 --> 00:46:11,598
The mind protects itself
the best way it knows how.

920
00:46:11,835 --> 00:46:13,128
There!

921
00:46:13,337 --> 00:46:14,672
Wait. One more.

922
00:46:14,672 --> 00:46:15,346
Ow.

923
00:46:20,135 --> 00:46:21,762
What are your intentions
toward Ysa?

924
00:46:21,787 --> 00:46:24,415
Ysa and I only became
friends yesterday.

925
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,690
Are we friends now?

926
00:46:25,815 --> 00:46:26,899
Uh—why not?

927
00:46:30,729 --> 00:46:31,729
Oh!

928
00:46:33,440 --> 00:46:34,692
- I didn't mean to—
- You're paying for this!

929
00:46:34,692 --> 00:46:35,943
How am I supposed
to sell this now?

930
00:46:35,968 --> 00:46:36,924
Pay up!
